@node Top
@top typst-watch

typst-watch starts a buffer-local @command{typst watch} process for
Typst buffers and opens generated PDFs in a configurable viewer.

@menu
* Installation::
* Usage::
* Configuration::
* Development::
@end menu

@node Installation
@chapter Installation

Place typst-watch.el on your load-path, then load it:

@lisp
(require 'typst-watch)
@end lisp

Enable automatic watching for Typst buffers:

@lisp
(typst-watch-auto-mode 1)
@end lisp

@node Usage
@chapter Usage

Use @kbd{M-x typst-watch-mode} to start or stop a buffer-local
@command{typst watch} process.

The main commands are:

@table @asis
@item typst-watch-start
Start @command{typst watch} for the current file.

@item typst-watch-stop
Stop the buffer-local watch process.

@item typst-watch-compile
Run @command{typst compile} and open the output PDF.

@item typst-watch-preview
Open the current output PDF.

@item typst-watch-compile-and-preview
Compile the current file and open the output PDF.
@end table

typst-watch-mode binds @kbd{C-c ! w} to toggle the watcher,
@kbd{C-c ! c} to compile, and @kbd{C-c ! p} to preview.

When typst-watch-auto-mode is enabled, typst-ts-compile,
typst-ts-preview, and typst-ts-compile-and-preview open the PDF
viewer after they run, when those commands are available.

@node Configuration
@chapter Configuration

Set typst-watch-pdf-viewer to force a viewer:

@lisp
(setq typst-watch-pdf-viewer "zathura")
@end lisp

When typst-watch-pdf-viewer is nil, typst-watch tries @command{zathura}
and then @command{evince}.  Change the fallback with
typst-watch-fallback-pdf-viewer.

Set typst-watch-typst-command when Typst is not on PATH.

Set typst-watch-output-file-function to customise the output PDF path.
The function receives the Typst source path and must return the PDF path.

@node Development
@chapter Development

Run the full local gate:

@example
make all
@end example

This byte-compiles the package with warnings as errors, runs the ERT tests,
runs checkdoc, and builds this info manual.

@bye
